	"LauncherChangelog": "Upgraded from `.NET 9.0` to `.NET 10.0`, which will require you to download the new runtime if you only have `.NET 9.0` installed.\nRewrote how dll injection is handled, it is much safer with more detailed error reporting, and it also now uses `LoadLibraryW` instead of `LoadLibraryA`.\nThe prevent injection if EAC is detected setting is now disabled by default for new users, injection will just fail gracefully if attempted to inject with EAC.\nRemoved the `Launch Rocket League` button to avoid confusion, as it required the user to manually put `-noeac` in their launch parameters.\nFixed the process status being stuck saying `East Anti-Cheat Detected` instead of saying if rocket league is running or not.\nIncreased the default injection time for new users from `2500` to `3500`.",
	"ModuleChangelog": "Overlay windows no longer render on top of each other if you have multiple set to the same corner position on your screen.\nAdded a new setting `training_ball_max_speed`, which lets you override the max ball speed in custom training packs.\nAdded a new setting `imgui_scanner_copy_origin` to the function scanner, which will include origin names when copying them to your clipboard.\nAdded a new setting `imgui_scanner_copy_calls` to the function scanner, which will include call amounts when copying them to your clipboard.\nAdded four new settings for custom styles, `LightMode`, `ImageRounding`, `DragDropTargetRounding`, and `DragDropTargetPadding`.\nRenamed the `imgui_scanner_flags` setting to `imgui_scanner_copy_flags` for consistency reasons.\nFixed an instance where the `interface_disable_eac_popup` setting didn't work if you injected too late.",
